{title: 496 - Eternal Love, We Have No Good}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Christian Life}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[F]Eternal [C7/G]Love, we [Am]have no [Abdim]good to [C7/G]bring Thee,
[F]No [Dm]single [C/E]good [F]of [C/E]all [Dm]our hands [C/G]have [Gm]wrought,
[F]No [C7/G]worthy music [Am]have [F/A]we found to [C7/Bb]sing [Bb]Thee,
[Gm]No [Am/C]jewelled word, no [Bb]quick up [F/C]soaring thought.

Verse 2:
[F]And [C7/G]yet [F/A]we [C7/G]come; and [Am]when our [Abdim]faith would [C7/G]falter
[F]Show [Dm]us, O [C/E]Love, [F]the [Dm]quiet place [C/G]of [Gm]prayer,
[F]The [C7/G]golden censer [Am]and [F/A]the golden [C7/Bb]altar,
[Gm]And [Am/C]the [C7/Bb]great [Am]angel [Bb]waiting [F/C]for [C7]us [F]there.
